From b4b88f030de42e8f8cbc34233aa594279484c1f0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: r-chong <dev.reese.chong@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 20:46:38 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] feat(models-torch): Engine-managed paged KV for Muse Glimmer
 via Resin CacheLayout

Declare a two-group CacheLayout (13 full-attention layers as HISTORY, 39
sliding layers as WINDOW with read window 2048; 39 = 3 x 13 so one slab holds
one window block or three history blocks), size the pool with
plan_cache_capacity, bind via CachePoolBinding, and route Engine plans through
a page-table attention path. The request-owned path stays as kv_cache='local'.
CPU tests run a tiny Muse-shaped model through the real Engine in both modes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
